{
  "0": [
    {
      "text": "Silver rounds and silver coins look identical.",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 2.952316384180791
    },
    {
      "text": "Both are one troy ounce of .",
      "startSec": 2.802316384180791,
      "endSec": 4.599378531073446
    },
    {
      "text": "999 fine silver.",
      "startSec": 4.599378531073446,
      "endSec": 5.626271186440678
    },
    {
      "text": "The only difference is who minted them, and that one fact can cost you 20 percent more.",
      "startSec": 5.626271186440678,
      "endSec": 11.36
    }
  ],
  "1": [
    {
      "text": "Silver rounds from private mints carry the lowest premiums of any one-ounce silver product.",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 4.892631578947368
    },
    {
      "text": "You are looking at 3 to 8 percent over spot in normal market conditions.",
      "startSec": 4.742631578947368,
      "endSec": 8.613724696356273
    },
    {
      "text": "No government program overhead, no dealer exclusivity, no collector markup baked in.",
      "startSec": 8.613724696356273,
      "endSec": 13.28
    }
  ],
  "2": [
    {
      "text": "The American Silver Eagle is the most recognized silver coin in the USA.",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 4.428387096774194
    },
    {
      "text": "It is also the most expensive to buy.",
      "startSec": 4.2783870967741935,
      "endSec": 6.554086021505377
    },
    {
      "text": "In normal markets you are paying 15 to 25 percent over spot.",
      "startSec": 6.554086021505377,
      "endSec": 10.24440860215054
    },
    {
      "text": "During supply crunches like 2021 and 2022, that premium climbed above 50 percent.",
      "startSec": 10.24440860215054,
      "endSec": 15.226344086021507
    },
    {
      "text": "Same silver.",
      "startSec": 15.226344086021507,
      "endSec": 15.96440860215054
    },
    {
      "text": "Much higher cost.",
      "startSec": 15.96440860215054,
      "endSec": 17.16
    }
  ],
  "3": [
    {
      "text": "Canadian Silver Maple Leafs cost less than American Silver Eagles but more than rounds.",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 4.810588235294117
    },
    {
      "text": "Typical premiums run 10 to 18 percent over spot.",
      "startSec": 4.660588235294116,
      "endSec": 7.31470588235294
    },
    {
      "text": "They are universally recognized, .",
      "startSec": 7.31470588235294,
      "endSec": 9.19470588235294
    },
    {
      "text": "9999 fine silver, and resell easily worldwide.",
      "startSec": 9.19470588235294,
      "endSec": 11.738235294117645
    },
    {
      "text": "The premium is the tradeoff you pay for that recognition.",
      "startSec": 11.738235294117645,
      "endSec": 15.04
    }
  ],
  "4": [
    {
      "text": "Here is the part most buyers do not realize.",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 2.263630769230769
    },
    {
      "text": "Silver rounds and silver coins contain the same metal.",
      "startSec": 2.113630769230769,
      "endSec": 4.891723076923077
    },
    {
      "text": "Both are .",
      "startSec": 4.891723076923077,
      "endSec": 5.406184615384615
    },
    {
      "text": "999 fine silver.",
      "startSec": 5.406184615384615,
      "endSec": 6.229323076923077
    },
    {
      "text": "The Canadian Maple Leaf hits .",
      "startSec": 6.229323076923077,
      "endSec": 7.7727076923076925
    },
    {
      "text": "9999, slightly higher, but the difference is negligible for a physical reserve.",
      "startSec": 7.7727076923076925,
      "endSec": 11.836953846153847
    },
    {
      "text": "You are not getting better silver by paying a 20 percent premium on an Eagle versus a round.",
      "startSec": 11.836953846153847,
      "endSec": 16.72
    }
  ],
  "5": [
    {
      "text": "Let us do the math.",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 1.1478620689655172
    },
    {
      "text": "At a 30 dollar spot price, rounds cost about 31 to 32 dollars per ounce.",
      "startSec": 0.9978620689655172,
      "endSec": 5.347655172413793
    },
    {
      "text": "An American Silver Eagle costs 34 to 37 dollars.",
      "startSec": 5.347655172413793,
      "endSec": 8.24751724137931
    },
    {
      "text": "Over 100 ounces",
      "startSec": 8.24751724137931,
      "endSec": 9.153724137931034
    },
    {
      "text": "that gap is 300 to 600 dollars in extra premiums for the exact same amount of silver.",
      "startSec": 9.153724137931034,
      "endSec": 14.288896551724136
    },
    {
      "text": "That is real money for any serious reserve builder.",
      "startSec": 14.288896551724136,
      "endSec": 17.52
    }
  ],
  "6": [
    {
      "text": "This chart shows where your money actually goes when you choose a format.",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 4.779578947368421
    },
    {
      "text": "Rounds sit at 5 percent.",
      "startSec": 4.629578947368421,
      "endSec": 6.200947368421052
    },
    {
      "text": "Maple Leafs at 14.",
      "startSec": 6.200947368421052,
      "endSec": 7.3794736842105255
    },
    {
      "text": "Eagles at 20 or higher.",
      "startSec": 7.3794736842105255,
      "endSec": 8.88536842105263
    },
    {
      "text": "Same silver inside every bar.",
      "startSec": 8.88536842105263,
      "endSec": 10.784105263157894
    },
    {
      "text": "Different wrapper cost.",
      "startSec": 10.784105263157894,
      "endSec": 12.44
    }
  ],
  "7": [
    {
      "text": "Silver rounds will never develop collector value.",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 2.403184713375796
    },
    {
      "text": "Their price tracks spot price and nothing more.",
      "startSec": 2.2531847133757963,
      "endSec": 4.55828025477707
    },
    {
      "text": "Government coins are different.",
      "startSec": 4.55828025477707,
      "endSec": 6.078662420382166
    },
    {
      "text": "Rare American Silver Eagle proof sets and low-mintage years sell for far above their silver melt value.",
      "startSec": 6.078662420382166,
      "endSec": 11.130254777070064
    },
    {
      "text": "If you want numismatic upside alongside physical silver, rounds are not your answer.",
      "startSec": 11.130254777070064,
      "endSec": 15.4
    }
  ],
  "8": [
    {
      "text": "Building a reserve efficiently?",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 1.8109965635738832
    },
    {
      "text": "Buy rounds.",
      "startSec": 1.6609965635738833,
      "endSec": 2.30360824742268
    },
    {
      "text": "More silver per dollar, no premium overhead.",
      "startSec": 2.30360824742268,
      "endSec": 4.874054982817869
    },
    {
      "text": "Gifting recognizable silver?",
      "startSec": 4.874054982817869,
      "endSec": 6.50979381443299
    },
    {
      "text": "Buy government coins.",
      "startSec": 6.50979381443299,
      "endSec": 7.73659793814433
    },
    {
      "text": "Collecting?",
      "startSec": 7.73659793814433,
      "endSec": 8.379209621993127
    },
    {
      "text": "Coins only, rounds have no collector upside.",
      "startSec": 8.379209621993127,
      "endSec": 10.949656357388315
    },
    {
      "text": "Most serious buyers hold both.",
      "startSec": 10.949656357388315,
      "endSec": 12.702233676975943
    },
    {
      "text": "Rounds for bulk weight.",
      "startSec": 12.702233676975943,
      "endSec": 14.045876288659793
    },
    {
      "text": "A few rolls of Eagles for liquidity and gifting.",
      "startSec": 14.045876288659793,
      "endSec": 17
    }
  ],
  "9": [
    {
      "text": "Follow for more silver news.",
      "startSec": 0,
      "endSec": 2.36
    }
  ]
}